Backport upstream drm/panthor scheduler tick/rotation fixes to 6.12

On 6.12 the scheduler stops ticking whenever CSG slots are not all used,
or when any idle group is resident, so CSG slot priorities are never
rotated. Resident groups keep the slot priority they got at bind time,
and the CSF firmware serves the higher slot first. A busy ARC (PanVK)
group can keep Chrome's resident group off the shader cores for more
than JOB_TIMEOUT_MS (5 s), so Chrome's job times out and its context is
lost (GL_GUILTY_CONTEXT_RESET_KHR).

Upstream commits (v7.0, last one v7.2):
  a3c2d0b40b10 drm/panthor: Fix the full_tick check
  4356d21994f4 drm/panthor: Fix immediate ticking on a disabled tick
  61d9a43d70dc drm/panthor: Fix the logic that decides when to stop ticking
  55429c51d5db drm/panthor: Fix the group priority rotation logic
  36c5dff41fd9 drm/panthor: Kill panthor_sched_immediate_tick()
  99820b4b7e50 drm/panthor: Make sure we resume the tick when new jobs are submitted
               (context adjusted: 6.12 has no per-queue timeout rework)
  6fec8b473497 drm/panthor: Don't overrule pending immediate ticks in sched_resume_tick()

